<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Muria</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Muria people, Muria Gond</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Muria are a Gondi-speaking Adivasi people of the Bastar region of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chhattisgarh">Chhattisgarh</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>. They are known for the ghotul, a village dormitory where young people lived, learned and took part in community life, and for their dances and crafts. Like other Bastar communities, they kept close ritual ties with the goddess <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/danteshwari">Danteshwari</a> and the Rajas of Bastar.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/muria.jpg" alt="Muria" width="320" height="480" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Yves Picq http://veton.picq.fr/ · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Inde_muria_0510.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
